# This directory (~/Podman = /KoolApps/Podman) holds LIVE service data for several
# containers (Plex library/database, Home Assistant, Pi-hole, Syncthing, RustDesk)
# plus runtime logs. None of that should be committed.
#
# Strategy: deny everything by default, then whitelist only the Plex health-check
# system files. To track a new file you must add an explicit "!" rule below.

# Ignore everything at the repo root...
/*

# ...then re-include the health-check system:
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/PLEX-HEALTHCHECK.md
!/plex-healthcheck.sh
!/plex-healthcheck.service.example
!/plex-healthcheck.timer.example
!/plex-report-clear.sh
!/plex-report-clear.service.example
!/plex-report-clear.timer.example
!/test-cron-jobs.sh

# Allow descending into Plex/ to track only the sanitized Quadlet TEMPLATE,
# REMOTE-ACCESS.md (troubleshooting reference), and system service files.
# Ignores the live Plex config/database AND any real plex.container
# (the host-specific unit contains private addresses and must never be committed).
!/Plex/
/Plex/*
!/Plex/plex.container.example
!/Plex/REMOTE-ACCESS.md
!/Plex/plex-novpn.sh
!/Plex/plex-nat-loopback.service
!/Plex/99-plex-nat.conf

# Allow descending into Dispatcher/ to track the compose file and the sanitized
# systemd user-service TEMPLATE (rootless podman-compose). The live unit lives in
# ~/.config/systemd/user/ and is never committed.
!/Dispatcher/
/Dispatcher/*
!/Dispatcher/docker-compose.yml
!/Dispatcher/dispatcharr-compose.service.example
